  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🎮 Gamertag Generator",
      "tagline": "Gamertags and usernames: cool, funny, fantasy or short, with your own word mixed in if you like."
    },
    "intro": "A good gamertag is short, easy to read in a kill feed and still free on the platform you play on. This **gamertag generator** makes tags in four styles (cool, funny, fantasy and short four-letter tags) and can mix in a word or name of your own, so you end up with something that's yours.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Each platform's name rules",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Xbox:</strong> gamertags can be up to 12 characters and include spaces. Since 2019, if the name you want is taken, Xbox lets you keep it with a number suffix (like #1234) shown after it.</li><li><strong>Discord:</strong> since 2023, every account has a unique username of 2 to 32 characters, using lowercase letters, numbers, underscores and full stops, plus a separate display name that can be anything.</li><li><strong>Instagram:</strong> usernames can be up to 30 characters, with letters, numbers, full stops and underscores.</li><li><strong>TikTok:</strong> usernames can be up to 24 characters, with letters, numbers, underscores and full stops.</li></ul><p>Rules change from time to time, so check the platform's own sign-up page if a name won't go through.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "What makes a good gamertag",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Short.</strong> Teammates need to call it out in a hurry. Two parts at most.</li><li><strong>Readable.</strong> Avoid swapping letters for numbers (Sh4d0w) unless it's a joke; it's hard to say and easy to misspell.</li><li><strong>Yours.</strong> Add a word you actually like, a nickname or an in-joke, with <em>Include your own word</em>.</li><li><strong>Clean.</strong> Every name here is family-friendly, and platforms do remove offensive names.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "If your favourite is taken",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Add a number</strong> that means something to you, not a random one.</li><li><strong>Try another style.</strong> A fantasy tag (Runeblade) is less likely to be taken than a cool one (ShadowWolf).</li><li><strong>Go short.</strong> Four-letter tags are rare on old platforms but you'll often find an invented one free.</li></ul><p>For a character name rather than a tag, see the <a href=\"../categories/dnd-names.html\">D&amp;D</a> and <a href=\"../categories/pop_culture-names.html\">pop culture</a> name generators.</p><p>Playing Minecraft? The <a href=\"minecraft-username-generator.html\">Minecraft Username Generator</a> only makes names that fit Minecraft's 3 to 16 character rules.</p><p>For an animal persona to go with your handle, try the <a href=\"fursona-name-generator.html\">Fursona Name Generator</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "How long can an Xbox gamertag be?",
        "answer": "Up to 12 characters, including spaces. If the name is already taken, Xbox adds a number suffix so you can still use it."
      },
      {
        "question": "What are Discord's username rules?",
        "answer": "Since 2023, usernames are unique, 2 to 32 characters, and use lowercase letters, numbers, underscores and full stops. Your display name can be different."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do I make a gamertag with my name in it?",
        "answer": "Choose \"Yes, use the word below\", type your name or nickname, and press Generate Names."
      }
    ]
